# Congress DEO lens: the index is rebuilt by analysis/web/buildCongressIndex.mjs
# from the (larger) comparison payload. The WebP portraits are pre-rendered and
# COMMITTED — they change only when the roster changes, and
# scripts/build_congress_portraits.py --check (hash-only, no Pillow) verifies
# staleness in CI. Run the builder without arguments to re-render after a
# roster or display-size change, then commit the result.
#analysis/data/congress_district_index_2027.json

# Location lens index for #congress?lens=location; derived from the DEO index,
# PSGC2LEG assignments + district polygons and the cleaned observations.
# Rebuilt by npm run generate:data:congress (analysis/web/buildLocationLens.py).
#analysis/data/location_district_index_2027.json

# District polygons joined to both lenses' figures for #congress/map; emitted
# by the same builder run as the location index.
#analysis/data/congress_district_map_2027.json

# FMR title/coordinate extraction and legislative lens; both are rebuilt by
# generate:data from the retained workbench and PSGC reference inputs.
#other-analysis/data/fmr_psgc_locations_2027.json
#analysis/data/fmr_legislative_index_2027.json

